$$
In Mott-Schottky analysis, the positive slope of UML-2 ascertains the $n$ -type electronic characteristic which is analogous to that of the parent MOFs [8,47]. The Carrier density was analyzed as per the Eq. (5):
$$
\frac{1}{c^{2}}=\frac{2}{\pmb{q}\in\in\varsigma_{0}N_{d}}\left(\pmb{E}-\pmb{E}_{f b}-\frac{K_{b}T}{\pmb{q}}\right)(\mathrm{n-type})
